If you’re reading this I will be or am already dead by suicide. I think anyone who cares deserves an explanation. Please let me explain. 

I was born on May 26th 2002 in Vynetsia, Ukraine. I was then adopted by my parents Brad and Mary Jane Henderson. My Mom and Dad had unrealistic expectations of what having a child was like and I was punished my whole life for that. My parents sent me to psychiatrists because when I was younger I didn’t follow directions. I was put on medication which is one the biggest reasons I am dead or soon will be, psychiatric drugs kill millions but I will explain and provide evidence for that later. In high school I had a 4.1 GPA and my parents did the 3 things that lead to my death. The first was not letting go into AP classes. I can remember having close to a religious experience by the washing machine when after pleading with my parents to sign the form they said no. My faith in education and institutions was destroyed first and at that point they were further destroyed by everything after. The second was not getting me a car when I was 16. I wanted to become financially independent but getting a job is impossible without a car(My parents don’t believe this very obvious true fact). The third thing my parents did that lead to my death was preventing me from going to the colleges I wanted to go to. I was given a choice of 3 schools even though I could have possibly got into Columbia, or NYU, or Cornell, or many other very good schools that would have provided an edge in the absurd capitalism job market. At 24 with a physics degree, no car, 900+ job applications with no response, the future that I predicted has come true. I can’t even get hired at Dunkin Donuts. As for psychiatry they are equally to blame as my parents. Psychiatry is built on a western lie, that human psychological suffering is medical. It is not and never will be the case. They commit violence that kills people. My best friend also died the same way I did on September 3rd. https://macfaddenfuneralhome.com/tribute/details/1203/Joseph-Phillips-V/obituary.html 
Look obviously everyone involved in this doesn’t know any better. My parents don’t know any better and neither do the psychiatrists. But what people need is not hard. They need community, good material conditions(transportation, housing, food, disposal income, etc.) and they need meaningful relationships both romantic and platonic. We live under a mode of production where me and my friend were deprived of some of these things at every turn of our existence. I tried really hard to change my material conditions but I can’t. My parents refuse to even get me an 800 dollar car when they live in a big house in North Carolina that they bought in cash. Please don’t blame yourself. Just please honor me by taking care of one another and abolish psychiatry.

I love you all,
Chris Henderson
